+# Stack Installer P1 macOS Operator Runbook
+
+Status: local handoff for the buddy MacBook Pro proof window.
+
+## Handoff Contents
+
+- Single transfer bundle:
+  `stack-installer-p1-macos-handoff-cedc46b905.tgz`
+- Transfer bundle checksum:
+  `stack-installer-p1-macos-handoff-cedc46b905.tgz.sha256`
+- Quick start:
+  `START_HERE.md`
+- Return note:
+  `RETURN_THIS_FILE.md`
+- Source archive:
+  `beep-effect6-stack-installer-p1-macos-source-cedc46b905.tgz`
+- Guided proof runner:
+  `RUN_MAC_PROOF.sh`
+- Source HEAD: `cedc46b905`
+- Source archive shape: shallow Git checkout, so `git status` and repo
+  postinstall hooks work after extraction.
+- Coordinator branch: `feat/stack-installer-p1-live`
+- Expected returned bundle:
+  `output/stack-installer/p1-live/stack-installer-p1-macos.tgz`
+
+Do not paste or record a plaintext Discord token, 1Password secret, provider
+credential, upload token, or account password. The Discord bot token must enter
+the proof only as an `op://vault/item/field` reference.
+
+## Values To Have Ready
+
+- Discord guild ID, or a 1Password reference that resolves to it
+- Discord channel ID, or a 1Password reference that resolves to it
+- Discord channel display name, or a 1Password reference that resolves to it
+- Discord bot token 1Password reference shaped like `op://vault/item/field`
+- operator label, defaulting to `operator-macos-001`
+- deterministic test message, defaulting to `Stack Installer P1 macOS proof`
+
+The bot token reference must point to the bot token field, not the guild ID or
+channel ID field.
+
+The guided runner verifies the refs before recording starts. It stops early if
+the display name resolves to only digits or the bot token ref resolves to a
+Discord ID-shaped value.
+
+## 1. Expand The Handoff And Source Archive
+
+Copy `stack-installer-p1-macos-handoff-cedc46b905.tgz` and
+`stack-installer-p1-macos-handoff-cedc46b905.tgz.sha256` to the Mac, then run:
+
+```bash
+mkdir -p ~/stack-installer-p1-handoff
+cp stack-installer-p1-macos-handoff-cedc46b905.tgz* ~/stack-installer-p1-handoff/
+cd ~/stack-installer-p1-handoff
+shasum -a 256 -c stack-installer-p1-macos-handoff-cedc46b905.tgz.sha256
+tar -xzf stack-installer-p1-macos-handoff-cedc46b905.tgz
+```
+
+Then expand the source archive:
+
+```bash
+mkdir -p ~/stack-installer-p1-macos
+cp RUN_MAC_PROOF.sh ~/stack-installer-p1-macos/
+tar -xzf beep-effect6-stack-installer-p1-macos-source-cedc46b905.tgz \
+  -C ~/stack-installer-p1-macos
+cd ~/stack-installer-p1-macos/beep-effect6-stack-installer-p1-macos-cedc46b905
+cp ../RUN_MAC_PROOF.sh .
+chmod +x RUN_MAC_PROOF.sh
+```
+
+Fast path after tools and account auth are ready:
+
+```bash
+./RUN_MAC_PROOF.sh --help
+./RUN_MAC_PROOF.sh
+```
+
+The script prompts for the Discord IDs, channel display name, operator label,
+test message, and the `op://...` token reference. The Discord IDs and display
+name can be literal values or `op://...` references; the runner resolves them
+locally without printing them. It runs preflight, capture, checksums, local
+audit, and packaging. Use the manual sections below only if you need to run the
+proof one command at a time.
+
+## 2. Install Missing Tools Only As Needed
+
+Probe first:
+
+```bash
+command -v git
+command -v bun
+command -v cargo
+command -v op
+command -v claude
+command -v codex
+```
+
+Install only what is missing. Useful current macOS entry points:
+
+```bash
+xcode-select -p || xcode-select --install
+command -v bun || curl -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash
+command -v cargo || curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh -s -- -y
+command -v op || brew install 1password-cli
+command -v claude || curl -fsSL https://claude.ai/install.sh | bash
+command -v npm || brew install node
+command -v codex || npm i -g @openai/codex
+```
+
+If Homebrew is not already installed, use the official 1Password manual
+installer instead of spending the proof window debugging Homebrew. Claude Code
+also supports `brew install --cask claude-code` when Homebrew is already ready.
+
+After installing Bun, Rust, Claude Code, or Codex, open a new terminal window
+or source the shell profile before rerunning the probes:
+
+```bash
+source ~/.zshrc 2>/dev/null || true
+source ~/.zprofile 2>/dev/null || true
+```
+
+## 3. Authenticate With User Accounts
+
+Authenticate before starting the screen recording:
+
+```bash
+op signin
+claude
+codex
+```
+
+Then verify status:
+
+```bash
+op whoami
+claude auth status
+codex login status
+```
+
+Stop here if `op`, `claude`, or `codex` cannot authenticate.
+
+## 4. Preflight The Checkout
+
+```bash
+git status --short --branch
+bun install
+bun run config-sync:check
+(cd apps/stack-installer && bun run build)
+(cd apps/stack-installer/src-tauri && cargo check)
+```
+
+## 5. Fill Runtime Values
+
+Use the real Discord target values from the user. The guided runner can accept
+1Password references for the guild ID, channel ID, and display name. If you run
+this manual path, resolve those non-token values before exporting them. Keep the
+token as an `op://...` reference only.
+
+```bash
+export STACK_INSTALLER_PLATFORM=macos
+export STACK_INSTALLER_OPERATOR_LABEL=operator-macos-001
+export STACK_INSTALLER_DISCORD_GUILD_ID='<discord-guild-id>'
+export STACK_INSTALLER_DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID='<discord-channel-id>'
+export STACK_INSTALLER_DISCORD_CHANNEL_DISPLAY_NAME='<discord-channel-display-name>'
+export STACK_INSTALLER_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN_REFERENCE='op://<vault>/<item>/<field>'
+export STACK_INSTALLER_TEST_MESSAGE='Stack Installer P1 macOS proof'
+
+export STACK_INSTALLER_REQUEST_JSON="$(bun --print '
+JSON.stringify({
+  targetPlatform: process.env.STACK_INSTALLER_PLATFORM,
+  operatorLabel: process.env.STACK_INSTALLER_OPERATOR_LABEL,
+  discordGuildId: process.env.STACK_INSTALLER_DISCORD_GUILD_ID,
+  discordChannelId: process.env.STACK_INSTALLER_DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID,
+  discordChannelDisplayName: process.env.STACK_INSTALLER_DISCORD_CHANNEL_DISPLAY_NAME,
+  discordBotTokenReference: process.env.STACK_INSTALLER_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN_REFERENCE,
+  testMessageContent: process.env.STACK_INSTALLER_TEST_MESSAGE
+})
+')"
+```
+
+## 6. Record And Capture The macOS Proof
+
+Create the output directory:
+
+```bash
+mkdir -p output/stack-installer/p1-live/macos
+```
+
+Start macOS screen recording with `Shift+Command+5`. Record only the terminal
+proof window. Do not show password prompts, 1Password item values, provider
+account secrets, browser account pages, or Discord bot-token pages.
+
+Run the proof:
+
+```bash
+cd apps/stack-installer
+bun run p1:proof:capture -- --request-json "$STACK_INSTALLER_REQUEST_JSON"
+```
+
+Stop the screen recording and move the resulting `.mov` into the proof
+directory:
+
+```bash
+cd ../..
+ls -lt ~/Desktop/*.mov
+mv ~/Desktop/<recording-file>.mov output/stack-installer/p1-live/macos/screencast.mov
+```
+
+If the recording saved somewhere else, move that file instead.
+
+## 7. Checksum, Audit, And Package
+
+```bash
+cd apps/stack-installer
+bun run p1:proof:checksums -- --platform macos
+bun run p1:proof:audit -- --platform macos
+
+cd ../..
+tar -czf output/stack-installer/p1-live/stack-installer-p1-macos.tgz \
+  -C output/stack-installer/p1-live \
+  macos
+```
+
+Transfer only this returned bundle back to the coordinator by AirDrop, USB, or
+local file share:
+
+```text
+output/stack-installer/p1-live/stack-installer-p1-macos.tgz
+```
+
+## 8. Cleanup
+
+Before handing the Mac back, sign out of any user accounts that should not
+remain on the machine, including 1Password CLI/app, Claude Code, Codex, browser
+sessions, and Discord web sessions used during the proof.
+
+## Coordinator Intake After Return
+
+On the coordinator machine, place the returned bundle under
+`output/stack-installer/p1-live/`, then run:
+
+```bash
+cd apps/stack-installer
+bun run p1:proof:intake -- --output-root ../../output/stack-installer/p1-live
+bun run p1:proof:audit -- --platform macos
+bun run p1:proof:status -- --output-root ../../output/stack-installer/p1-live
+```
